1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:06,393
In 2005, the Cassini spacecraft was exploring

2
00:00:06,393 --> 00:00:08,350
Saturn and its moons.

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,598
One of them was tiny.

4
00:00:11,598 --> 00:00:12,797
A ball of ice,

5
00:00:12,797 --> 00:00:16,050
barely five hundred kilometres across.

6
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,584
Then Cassini looked at its south pole,

7
00:00:20,584 --> 00:00:23,075
and saw something no one expected.

8
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:25,970
Jets of water,

9
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:27,977
spraying out into space.

10
00:00:27,977 --> 00:00:29,900
This is the real image.

11
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,069
Beneath the ice,

12
00:00:33,069 --> 00:00:36,081
Cassini's data point to a global ocean

13
00:00:36,081 --> 00:00:37,350
of liquid water.

14
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:40,805
And in that spray,

15
00:00:40,805 --> 00:00:41,975
there was salt.

16
00:00:41,975 --> 00:00:44,550
Organic molecules. Even hydrogen.

17
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:47,874
Here on Earth,

18
00:00:47,874 --> 00:00:50,525
that combination means something.

19
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,242
In 1977, scientists exploring the dark floor

20
00:00:57,242 --> 00:00:59,974
of the Pacific found hot springs,

21
00:00:59,974 --> 00:01:02,374
and life crowded around them,

22
00:01:02,374 --> 00:01:04,775
where sunlight never reaches.

23
00:01:06,225 --> 00:01:08,709
Microbes there don't need the Sun.

24
00:01:08,709 --> 00:01:10,389
They feed on chemistry:

25
00:01:10,389 --> 00:01:12,143
hydrogen from the rocks,

26
00:01:12,143 --> 00:01:13,750
carbon from the water.

27
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:18,180
If the same chemistry is at work

28
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:21,446
inside Enceladus, is something living there

29
00:01:21,446 --> 00:01:21,750
too?
